    {
      "id": "VERDICT-008",
      "title": "FRESHNESS: another ticket's verdict is refused even on the right path",
      "note": "A verdict is evidence only for the run that produced it \u2014 copying a clean one into place must not open the gate.",
      "files": [
        {
          "base": "ticket",
          "path": "phases/code/iter-1-verdict.json",
          "fixture": "verdict/stale-ticket.json"
        }
      ],
      "invoke": {
        "argv": [
          "verdict",
          "show",
          "--ticket",
          "TKT-1",
          "--skill",
          "code",
          "--iteration",
          "1"
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "exit_code": 2,
        "stderr_contains": [
          "verdict ticket_id is 'TKT-9' but this is 'TKT-1'",
          "a verdict is evidence only for the run that produced it"
        ]
      },
      "severity": "critical"
    },
    {
      "id": "VERDICT-009",
      "title": "FRESHNESS: `verdict show` refuses a verdict from another iteration",
      "files": [
        {
          "base": "ticket",
          "path": "phases/code/iter-3-verdict.json",
          "fixture": "verdict/stale-iteration.json"
        }
      ],
      "invoke": {
        "argv": [
          "verdict",
          "show",
          "--ticket",
          "TKT-1",
          "--skill",
          "code",
          "--iteration",
          "3"
        ]
      },
      "expect": {
        "exit_code": 2,
        "stderr_contains": [
          "not usable",
          "verdict iteration is 1 but this is 3",
          "a verdict is evidence only for the run that produced it"
        ],
        "stdout_excludes": [
          "\"passed\"",
          "\"ok\""
        ]
      },
      "severity": "critical",
      "note": "Was a known_divergence through v0.4.9: cmd_verdict_show called validate_verdict without `skill` or `iteration`, so a document whose own iteration was 1 read as a clean pass at iteration 3's path. MAR-573 passes both arguments through, closing it. The case now pins the rule instead of the gap \u2014 it asserts the refusal reaches stderr AND that no passing verdict leaks to stdout, because the original defect's harm was a body reporting passed:true, not the exit code alone."
    },
